; apps/web's build/lint scripts use POSIX shell syntax ($?, exit $var, left-associative
; ||/&&). npm's Windows default (cmd.exe) groups "A || B && C" as "A || (B && C)", so a
; successful first command silently skips EVERYTHING after it - measured 2026-09-07:
; `node tools/generate-llms.js || true && vite build ...` built nothing, exit 0, no error.
script-shell=C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\bash.exe
